 "stimulus_html": "<p>For the following exercises, use this information: Children from five families—the Chorro family, the Eswaran family, the Javernick family, the Lahde family, and the Stolly family—joined a town-wide Easter egg hunt. When they returned with their baskets, they had 827 eggs! They decided to share their eggs among the families based on the number of children in each family, as shown in the table below.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Family</th>\n<th>Number of Children</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>(C) Chorro</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(E) Eswaran</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(J) Javernick</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(L) Lahde</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(S) Stolly</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
